    {
      "title": "Integra 1530, 1560, 1580 – Communications Guide",
      "version": "Issue 1, Jan 2006",
      "url": "https://arccontrol.ccontrols.com/support/dp/Integra15xx.pdf",
      "note": "sections 1.2 (input registers) and 1.3 (holding registers)"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU over RS485, address 1 to 247 (no broadcast). 2400 to 19200 baud. Function 04 reads input registers, 03 reads and 16 writes holding registers. At most 40 parameters per request; up to 150 ms before the reply.",
    "Every value is an IEEE 754 float in two registers, most significant register first by default (see Register order, holding register 40041).",
    "The manual gives 3X/4X register numbers and the address bytes; the map uses the address bytes, as sent.",
    "Settings marked r/wp need the password written to holding register 40025 first.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 0,
  "x_status": "official",
